[0.044956, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m  Mental Health Knowledge Graph\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  Which help exists — for whom, in what language, at what price,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  and is there anyone actually there to provide it?\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[1.211463, "o", "  \u001b[1m113,710\u001b[0m nodes   \u001b[1m1,665,153\u001b[0m edges   \u001b[1m4\u001b[0m sources\r\n"]
[4.711801, "o", "\r\n\u001b[2m  [provenance]\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[33m  1. Where did this data come from, and how old is it?\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[4.711935, "o", "\u001b[2m  Before any answer is worth trusting. The graph records its own sources,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  when each was fetched and how often it moves — so it answers this itself\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  rather than asking you to take a caption on trust.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[36mMATCH (d:DataSource)\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mRETURN d.name AS source, d.publisher AS publisher,\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36md.fetched_on AS fetched, d.real_data AS real_data\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[6.465629, "o", "  \u001b[1msource             publisher                 fetched     real_data\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m-----------------  ------------------------  ----------  ---------\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[6.466024, "o", "  Synthea            The MITRE Corporation     2026-08-12  false    \r\n  NPPES              CMS / National Plan and…  2026-08-13  true     \r\n  HRSA               Health Resources and Se…  2026-08-13  true     \r\n"]
[6.466117, "o", "  FindTreatment.gov  SAMHSA / BHSIS            2026-08-10  true     \r\n\r\n  \u001b[32m3 ms\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[9.968753, "o", "\r\n\u001b[2m  [level 1 — one label]\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[33m  2. How much help exists across the country?\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  Every US behavioural-health facility, by the kind of care it provides.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  A spreadsheet answers this. It is the floor, not the argument.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[36mMATCH (f:Facility)-[:HAS_TYPE]->(t:FacilityType)\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mRETURN t.name AS care_type, count(f) AS facilities\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mORDER BY facilities DESC\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[11.718249, "o", "  \u001b[1mcare_type                facilities\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m-----------------------  ----------\u001b[0m\r\n  Mental health treatment  11,873    \r\n  Substance use treatment  11,420    \r\n\r\n  \u001b[32m1 ms\u001b[0m"]
[11.718368, "o", "\r\n"]
[15.218682, "o", "\r\n\u001b[2m  [level 2 — a join]\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[33m  3. Which states serve survivors of partner violence — and which barely do?\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  6,072 facilities nationally are tagged as serving survivors of partner\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  violence. The same question asked from both ends is the first hint that\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[15.219048, "o", "\u001b[2m  a national number hides the thing that matters.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[36mMATCH (f:Facility)-[:OFFERS]->(s:Service)\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mWHERE s.value = \"Clients who have experienced intimate partner violence, domestic violence\"\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mRETURN f.state AS state, count(f) AS ipv_facilities\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mORDER BY ipv_facilities DESC LIMIT 5\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[16.976971, "o", "  \u001b[1mstate  ipv_facilities\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m-----  --------------\u001b[0m\r\n  CA     563           \r\n  NY     427           \r\n  FL     296           \r\n  OH     286           \r\n  MD     242           \r\n\r\n  \u001b[32m8 ms\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[16.977082, "o", "  \u001b[36mMATCH (f:Facility)-[:OFFERS]->(s:Service)\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mWHERE s.value = \"Clients who have experienced intimate partner violence, domestic violence\"\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mRETURN f.state AS state, count(f) AS ipv_facilities\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mORDER BY ipv_facilities ASC LIMIT 5\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[18.735718, "o", "  \u001b[1mstate  ipv_facilities\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m-----  --------------\u001b[0m\r\n  VI     1             \r\n"]
[18.735787, "o", "  RI     13            \r\n  DC     18            \r\n  AK     20            \r\n  ND     21            \r\n\r\n  \u001b[32m9 ms\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[22.236108, "o", "\r\n\u001b[2m  [the question a survivor actually asks]\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[33m  4. Someone in Vermont needs trauma care after partner violence. Is there any?\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  Not a count — a place, a town and a number to call. This is the whole\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  point of the graph: the answer a helpline gives today is one national\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  number, because nobody has joined these fields together.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[36mMATCH (f:Facility)-[:OFFERS]->(t:Service), (f)-[:OFFERS]->(a:Service)\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mWHERE t.value = \"Trauma-related counseling\"\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[22.236213, "o", "  \u001b[36mAND a.value = \"Clients who have experienced intimate partner violence, domestic violence\"\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mAND f.state = \"VT\"\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mRETURN DISTINCT f.name AS facility, f.city AS town,\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mcoalesce(f.intake, f.phone) AS call\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mLIMIT 6\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[24.001083, "o", "  \u001b[1mfacility                                town                  call        \u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m--------------------------------------  --------------------  ------------\u001b[0m\r\n  BAART Programs                          Saint Johnsbury       802-748-6166\r\n  BAART Programs                          Saint Albans          802-370-3545\r\n  SaVida Health                           Newport               802-487-0781\r\n  CT Valley Addiction Recovery Inc        White River Junction  802-674-9400\r\n  SaVida Health                           Bennington            802-448-5105\r\n  Healthcare and Rehabilitation Services  Bellows Falls         855-220-9430\r\n\r\n  \u001b[32m15 ms\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[27.501295, "o", "\r\n\u001b[2m  [the follow-up nobody can answer]\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[33m  5. ...and is there anyone licensed to actually deliver it there?\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  A facility in a directory is a building. This is the second federal\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  register, joined on the state: who holds a licence in Vermont, and in\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  what. NPPES is authoritative for who is licensed — not for where they\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  practise today, since 71% of these records are over three years old.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[36mMATCH (p:Provider)-[:HAS_TAXONOMY]->(t:Taxonomy), (p)-[:PRACTICES_IN]->(s:State)\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mWHERE s.code = \"VT\" AND p.is_organization = false\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mRETURN t.classification AS speciality, count(p) AS clinicians\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[27.501335, "o", "  \u001b[36mORDER BY clinicians DESC LIMIT 5\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[29.407286, "o", "  \u001b[1mspeciality              clinicians\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m----------------------  ----------\u001b[0m\r\n  Counselor               2,102     \r\n  Social Worker           1,386     \r\n  Psychologist            686       \r\n  Psychiatry & Neurology  243       \r\n  Nurse Practitioner      142       \r\n"]
[29.40741, "o", "\r\n  \u001b[32m156 ms\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[36mMATCH (p:Provider)-[:HAS_TAXONOMY]->(t:Taxonomy), (p)-[:PRACTICES_IN]->(s:State)\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mWHERE s.code = \"VT\" AND p.is_organization = false\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mRETURN p.name AS clinician, p.city AS town, t.classification AS speciality\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mLIMIT 4\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[31.322932, "o", "  \u001b[1mclinician               town               speciality            \u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m----------------------  -----------------  ----------------------\u001b[0m\r\n  MILTON MARASCH          BURLINGTON         Psychologist          \r\n  LISA CATAPANO-FRIEDMAN  BENNINGTON         Psychiatry & Neurology\r\n  CAROL LOEFFLER          MANCHESTER CENTER  Psychologist          \r\n"]
[31.322995, "o", "  DOUGLAS DENNETT         ESSEX JCT          Psychiatry & Neurology\r\n\r\n  \u001b[32m165 ms\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[34.823344, "o", "\r\n\u001b[2m  [level 4 — absence]\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[33m  6. She must not be sent to an opioid-only programme. Who is left?\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  138 facilities match before the exclusion, 127 after. The eleven removed\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  would turn her away at the door. An embedding cannot represent a service\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  a facility does not offer — absence is not a point in the space.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[34.823694, "o", "\r\n  \u001b[36mMATCH (f:Facility)-[:OFFERS]->(a:Service), (f)-[:OFFERS]->(t:Service)\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mWHERE a.value = \"Clients who have experienced intimate partner violence, domestic violence\"\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mAND t.value = \"Trauma-related counseling\" AND f.state = \"MA\"\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mWITH f OPTIONAL MATCH (f)-[:OFFERS]->(x:Service)\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mWHERE x.value = \"Opioid use disorder clients only\"\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[34.823971, "o", "  \u001b[36mWITH f, x\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mRETURN count(DISTINCT f.facility_id) AS before_exclusion,\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mcount(DISTINCT CASE WHEN x IS NULL THEN f.facility_id END) AS after_exclusion\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[36.589671, "o", "  \u001b[1mbefore_exclusion  after_exclusion\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m----------------  ---------------\u001b[0m\r\n  138               127            \r\n\r\n  \u001b[32m16 ms\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[36mMATCH (f:Facility)-[:OFFERS]->(a:Service), (f)-[:OFFERS]->(t:Service),\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36m(f)-[:OFFERS]->(sl:Service)\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mWHERE a.value = \"Clients who have experienced intimate partner violence, domestic violence\"\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mAND t.value = \"Trauma-related counseling\"\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mAND sl.value = \"Sliding fee scale (fee is based on income and other factors)\"\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mAND f.state = \"VT\"\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mWITH f OPTIONAL MATCH (f)-[:OFFERS]->(x:Service)\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mWHERE x.value = \"Opioid use disorder clients only\"\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mWITH f, x WHERE x IS NULL\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mRETURN DISTINCT f.name AS facility, f.city AS town,\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mcoalesce(f.intake, f.phone) AS call\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mLIMIT 4\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[38.365654, "o", "  \u001b[1mfacility                                town                  call        \u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m--------------------------------------  --------------------  ------------\u001b[0m\r\n  SaVida Health                           Newport               802-487-0781\r\n  CT Valley Addiction Recovery Inc        White River Junction  802-674-9400\r\n  SaVida Health                           Bennington            802-448-5105\r\n"]
[38.365782, "o", "  Healthcare and Rehabilitation Services  Bellows Falls         855-220-9430\r\n\r\n  \u001b[32m26 ms\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[41.865885, "o", "\r\n\u001b[2m  [four conditions, one building]\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[33m  7. She is leaving tonight and has nowhere to sleep.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  Survivor services, housing support and a 24-hour residential bed, all\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[41.866138, "o", "\u001b[2m  true of the same facility. In a normalised schema that is three\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  self-joins against 1.4 million service rows.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[36mMATCH (f:Facility)-[:OFFERS]->(a:Service), (f)-[:OFFERS]->(h:Service),\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36m(f)-[:OFFERS]->(r:Service)\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mWHERE a.value = \"Clients who have experienced intimate partner violence, domestic violence\"\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mAND h.value = \"Housing services\"\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mAND r.value = \"Residential/24-hour residential\"\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[41.866347, "o", "  \u001b[36mAND f.state = \"MA\"\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mRETURN DISTINCT f.name AS facility, f.city AS town,\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mcoalesce(f.intake, f.phone) AS call\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mLIMIT 5\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[43.633426, "o", "  \u001b[1mfacility            town         call              \u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m------------------  -----------  ------------------\u001b[0m\r\n  Megans House        Lowell       978-455-6973      \r\n  Dimock Center       Boston       617-442-8800 x1652\r\n  Steppingstone Inc   New Bedford  508-984-1880      \r\n  Catholic Charities  Worcester    508-797-6732      \r\n  Casa Esperanza Inc  Roxbury      857-998-1819      \r\n\r\n  \u001b[32m17 ms\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[47.133704, "o", "\r\n\u001b[2m  [a gap, not a ranking]\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[33m  8. A Deaf survivor needs an interpreter. Where is that hardest to find?\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[47.13405, "o", "\u001b[2m  Sign language is the single largest access need in this data — 6,023\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  facilities offer it — but it is not spread evenly. Asked from the thin\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  end, the question stops being a leaderboard and becomes a gap map.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[36mMATCH (f:Facility)-[:OFFERS]->(a:Service), (f)-[:OFFERS]->(t:Service),\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36m(f)-[:SPEAKS]->(l:Language)\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mWHERE a.value = \"Clients who have experienced intimate partner violence, domestic violence\"\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mAND t.value = \"Trauma-related counseling\"\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mAND l.name = \"Sign language services for the deaf and hard of hearing\"\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mRETURN f.state AS state, count(DISTINCT f.facility_id) AS facilities\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mORDER BY facilities ASC LIMIT 6\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[48.912725, "o", "  \u001b[1mstate  facilities\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m-----  ----------\u001b[0m\r\n  SD     2         \r\n  RI     2         \r\n  AR     3         \r\n  ND     4         \r\n  AK     5         \r\n  WY     6         \r\n\r\n  \u001b[32m29 ms\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[52.412921, "o", "\r\n\u001b[2m  [level 5 — the demand side]\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[33m  9. Who needs this help, and how many live where help is already scarce?\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  Supply is half a question. Synthea (MITRE, Apache 2.0) supplies a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  synthetic population — no real person is in this graph — and HRSA says\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  which counties are federally designated shortage areas. Neither\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  publisher joins to the other, and nobody publishes the intersection.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[36mMATCH (p:Patient)-[:HAS_CONDITION]->(c:Condition)\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mWHERE c.name = \"Victim of intimate partner abuse (finding)\"\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mRETURN p.state AS state, count(DISTINCT p.patient_id) AS survivors\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mORDER BY survivors DESC\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[54.174323, "o", "  \u001b[1mstate  survivors\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m-----  ---------\u001b[0m\r\n  MA     790      \r\n  VT     617      \r\n"]
[54.174448, "o", "\r\n  \u001b[32m11 ms\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[36mMATCH (p:Patient)-[:HAS_CONDITION]->(c:Condition),\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36m(p)-[:IN_COUNTY]->(ct:County),\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[54.174508, "o", "  \u001b[36m(sa:ShortageArea)-[:COVERS]->(ct)\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mWHERE c.name = \"Victim of intimate partner abuse (finding)\"\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mRETURN count(DISTINCT p.patient_id) AS survivors_in_a_shortage_area\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[55.951299, "o", "  \u001b[1msurvivors_in_a_shortage_area\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m----------------------------\u001b[0m\r\n  1,314                       \r\n\r\n  \u001b[32m27 ms\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[59.451463, "o", "\r\n\u001b[2m  [level 5 — all four sources]\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[33m  10. Where are survivors worst served, and is anyone there to help them?\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  The county they live in, how severe its federal designation is, how many\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  of them there are, and the clinical workforce of the state around them —\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  four datasets that no publisher joins, answered in one pass.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[36mMATCH (p:Patient)-[:HAS_CONDITION]->(cond:Condition),\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36m(p)-[:IN_COUNTY]->(ct:County)-[:IN_STATE]->(s:State),\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36m(sa:ShortageArea)-[:COVERS]->(ct)\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mWHERE cond.name = \"Victim of intimate partner abuse (finding)\"\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mRETURN s.code AS state, ct.name AS county, max(sa.score) AS worst_score,\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mcount(DISTINCT p.patient_id) AS survivors\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mORDER BY worst_score DESC LIMIT 5\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[61.235759, "o", "  \u001b[1mstate  county      worst_score  survivors\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m-----  ----------  -----------  ---------\u001b[0m\r\n  MA     Suffolk     23           86       \r\n"]
[61.23588, "o", "  MA     Essex       22           81       \r\n  MA     Berkshire   21           23       \r\n  MA     Middlesex   21           179      \r\n  VT     Chittenden  21           152      \r\n\r\n  \u001b[32m34 ms\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[36mMATCH (f:Facility)-[:OFFERS]->(a:Service),\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36m(f)-[:LOCATED_IN]->(s:State)-[h:HAS_PROVIDERS]->(t:Taxonomy)\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mWHERE a.value = \"Clients who have experienced intimate partner violence, domestic violence\"\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mAND t.code = \"2084P0800X\" AND s.code IN [\"MA\", \"VT\"]\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mRETURN s.code AS state, count(DISTINCT f.facility_id) AS ipv_facilities,\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mh.count AS psychiatrists\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mORDER BY ipv_facilities DESC\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[63.045635, "o", "  \u001b[1mstate  ipv_facilities  psychiatrists\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m-----  --------------  -------------\u001b[0m\r\n  MA     159             3,150        \r\n  VT     27              241          \r\n\r\n  \u001b[32m60 ms\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[66.545722, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[32m  One graph, four federal and simulated sources, one query language.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  Supply from FindTreatment.gov · shortage designations from HRSA ·\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  clinical capacity from NPPES · demand simulated with Synthea.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[2m  Public federal records only. No survivor, session or transcript is\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[66.545785, "o", "\u001b[2m  stored anywhere in this graph.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
